# .gitleaksignore — repo root (the CI gitleaks job runs `gitleaks git .` from here and reads this
# file by default). sec0914:history-carries-live-credentials-before-read-access.
#
# ONE fingerprint per verified finding, grouped under a comment header naming the class + a
# one-line reason. Four classes so far:
#   fixture / public-by-design / dead / false-positive — never live to begin with (heal round 1).
#   dead-with-evidence — a class A (live, history) / B (live, HEAD+history) / C (presumed live,
#     history) finding that WAS live, until the owner/orchestrator actually killed the credential
#     it names and could cite the proof (heal round 2) — added ONLY once that proof exists, never
#     speculatively, and never by this row's own author (the row measures + fixes the SCAN; the
#     owner/orchestrator kill the CREDENTIAL and are the ones who get to declare it dead).
# A finding with none of the above — still genuinely live, or simply not yet triaged — stays OUT of
# this file and keeps the scan RED. tools/history-secret-scan.mjs's own accountability check refuses
# any ignore line that sits under no class header at all.
#
# Fingerprint format: gitleaks git's own `commit:file:rule:startLine` (matches --report-format
# json/csv `Fingerprint` field byte for byte — never hand-typed, always copied from a real scan).

